<title>USA: USDA ups '98 US pork output forecast, exports unch.</title>
<headline>USDA ups '98 US pork output forecast, exports unch.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA raised Friday its estimate for 1998 U.S. pork production to 18.507 billion lbs from 18.357 billion lbs forecast in June, but left exports unchanged at 1.465 billion lbs.</p>
<p>In its monthly world supply and demand report, USDA said this summer's pig crop was expected to be a little larger than previously estimated and so the forecast for first quarter 1998 pork production was increased.</p>
<p>USDA also slightly increased its estimate for 1997 U.S. pork production to 17.151 billion lbs from 17.126 billion lbs seen in June. Exports remained at 1.250 billion lbs.</p>
</text>
